    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0278" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg204"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 29,1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> On the 30th ultimo, and on the 7th instant,
                    our consul at Nantes informed this department of suspicious circumstances in
                    regard to the iron-clad vessels Shanghai and San Francisco, which he has
                    reported to the legation at Paris. I will thank you to give your attention to
                    the matter, and to take such steps as may, in your judgment, be expedient,
                    towards preventing these vessels from falling into the hands of the
                    insurgents.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
